('011', 'charm_carnelian_leaf', 'Pair of carnelian leaf charms', 'Gemstone width: 12mm', 100.00, '["silver"]', '["carnelian"]', 'charm', 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 90),
('012', 'charm_druzy_leaf', 'Pair of druzy agate leaf charms', 'Druzy agate spheres, with natural crystals sparkling intermittently across their surfaces.\n\nGemstone width: 10mm, charm height: 18mm.', 100.00, '["silver"]', '["druzy agate"]', 'charm', 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 100),
('013', 'ring_copper_red_quartz', 'Red quartz and copper ring', 'A natural, untreated raw crystal of red quartz. It has been kept in the crystal-point shape in which it naturally formed, and set into a custom-made copper ring. Photos of the production process are included here.', NULL, '["copper"]', '["red quartz"]', 'ring', 6, 0, 1, 0, 0, 110),
('016', 'brooch_wood', 'Petrified wood brooch', 'This brooch holds agatised wood (ie. petrified as agate), with natural wood grain visible in creamy grey and dusky brick red. The stone is tightly secured in a sterling silver backing. The pin is also of sterling silver, and honed to a smooth blunted point to prevent damage to garments.\n\nThe stone originated in Petrified Forest National Park, Utah, USA. Ethically sourced; fair labour; cut and polished by hand; natural stone (not treated or enhanced).\n\nGemstone dimensions: 24x18mm (19 carats).', 300.00, '["silver"]', '["petrified wood","agate"]', 'brooch', 12, 0, 0, 0, 0, 120),
('018', 'pendant_copper_aventurine', 'Green aventurine pendant in copper', 'Natural, untreated 20mm green aventurine cabochon, set into a square copper basket setting. Aventurine is a form of quartz that contains small particles of mica, giving it a glittery effect.', NULL, '["copper"]', '["green aventurine"]', 'pendant', 2, 0, 1, 0, 0, 130),
('019', 'pendant_silver_cuprite', 'Cuprite pendant in sterling silver', 'This hand-cut piece of cuprite has been formed into a teardrop-shaped cabochon by an independent artisan. It has been set into a simple silver pendant with a hidden bail for threading a chain though. The distinctive forked prongs mirror the branched patterns running through the stone.', 210.00, '["silver"]', '["cuprite"]', 'pendant', 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 140),
('020', 'pendant_silver_rosequartz', 'Rose quartz pendant in sterling silver', 'Natural, untreated 18mm rose quartz cabochon in a sturdily-constructed basket setting.', 270.00, '["silver"]', '["rose quartz"]', 'pendant', 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 150),
('021', 'pendant_silver_aventurine_B', 'Green aventurine pendant in sterling silver', 'Natural, untreated 20mm green aventurine cabochon. The back of the pendant bears a teardrop design. Aventurine is a form of quartz that contains small particles of mica, giving it a sparkling effect, as though it were filled with glitter.', 300.00, '["silver"]', '["green aventurine"]', 'pendant', 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 160),
('022', 'pendant_silver_aventurine_A', 'Green aventurine pendant in sterling silver', 'Natural, untreated 20mm green aventurine cabochon. Aventurine is a form of quartz that contains small particles of mica, giving it a glittery effect.', 300.00, '["silver"]', '["green aventurine"]', 'pendant', 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 170),
('103', 'fibonacci_garnet', 'Pearl and garnet Fibonacci strand', 'Genuine untreated freshwater pearls and natural untreated rhodolite garnets, knotted by hand onto pure silk thread. Stones were selected in matched sets for symmetry. The mauve-pink of the freshwater pearls harmonises with the deep pink of the garnets.\n\nThe Fibonacci sequence of numbers can be found throughout nature, famously in the spirals of a sunflower or pinecone. It\'s reflected in this necklace: counting from the centre, on each side, the number of pearls between gemstones follows the pattern 1-2-3-5-8-13.\n\n(Please note: this pearl strand contains a small amount of adhesive, atypical in work produced by this workshop.)\n\nPearl diameter: 5.4mm, Finished length: 49cm', 410.00, '["silver"]', '["pearl","garnet"]', 'necklace', 8, 0, 0, 0, 0, 180),
('104', 'fibonacci_pietersite', 'Pearl and blue tiger eye Fibonacci strand', 'Genuine untreated freshwater pearls and natural untreated blue tiger eye (pietersite), knotted by hand onto pure silk thread. Stones were selected in matched pairs for symmetry.\n\nThe Fibonacci sequence of numbers can be found throughout nature, famously in the spirals of a sunflower or pinecone. It\'s reflected in this necklace: counting from the centre, on each side, the number of pearls between gemstones follows the pattern 1-2-3-5-8-13.\n\n(Please note: this pearl strand contains a small amount of adhesive, atypical in work produced by this workshop.)\n\nPearl diameter: 5.5mm, Finished length: 61.5cm', 490.00, '["silver"]', '["pearl","blue tiger eye","pietersite"]', 'necklace', 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 190),
('105', 'fibonacci_amethyst', 'Pearl and amethyst Fibonacci strand', 'Genuine freshwater pearls and natural untreated amethyst, knotted by hand onto pure silk thread. Stones were selected in matched sets for symmetry; the amethysts are darker at the centre, becoming lighter towards the top.\n\nThe Fibonacci sequence of numbers can be found throughout nature, famously in the spirals of a sunflower or pinecone. It\'s reflected in this necklace: counting from the centre, on each side, the number of pearls between gemstones follows the pattern 1-2-3-5-8-13.\n\nPearl diameter: 4.8mm, Finished length: 56cm', 480.00, '["silver"]', '["pearl","amethyst"]', 'necklace', 7, 0, 0, 0, 0, 200),
('023', 'pendant_silver_lab', 'Labradorite pendant in sterling silver', 'Natural, untreated 20mm labradorite cabochon, with nice chatoyancy. The back of the pendant bears a geometric design.', 390.00, '["silver"]', '["labradorite"]', 'pendant', 8, 0, 0, 0, 1, 210),
('024', 'Morenci_Chrysocolla', 'Morenci chrysocolla pendant in sterling silver', 'Chrysocolla from Morenci, Arizona has been hand-cut into a parabola-shaped cabochon by an independent artisan. It has been set into a circular basket setting pendant in sterling silver.', NULL, '["silver"]', '["chrysocolla"]', 'pendant', 5, 0, 1, 0, 0, 220),
('025', 'red_mica', 'Red mica in sterling silver basket setting', 'This natural, untreated red mica in quartz has been carved and polished by an independent artisan. Mica is the mineral that gives granite its sparkle. This piece is a deep red that shows off natural glitter deep within when turned in the light.', 370.00, '["silver"]', '["red mica","quartz"]', 'pendant', 10, 0, 0, 0, 1, 230),
('026', 'necklace_quartz', 'Quartz bead necklace on sterling silver', 'Sparkling iridescent-coated quartz beads have been hand-formed into sterling silver chain links. Beads measure 10mm at the center of the necklace and 8mm higher up on the chain. They are made from genuine quartz with an AB finish. Short for \'Aurora borealis\', this finish was invented by Swarovski in 1956, and is achieved by applying a microscopic-thin film of metal.', 430.00, '["silver"]', '["quartz"]', 'necklace', 8, 0, 0, 0, 1, 240),
('027', 'kyanite', 'Kyanite pendant strung on sterling silver', 'Kyanite is a mineral that forms long shimmering thread-like crystal structures. This piece has been strung through the top like a bead, held in place by geometric front and back plates that mirror the natural linear grain of the stone.', NULL, '["silver"]', '["kyanite"]', 'pendant', 7, 0, 1, 0, 0, 250);
